WEBVTT

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:36.160
All rise.

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:37.300
Bow.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.860
Yakisoba bread!

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.060
Hey! No running!

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:56.570
Lunch... Lunch...

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:59.220
It's a little early, Kiyori-chan.

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:02.160
Kazama.

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:07.740
Ka-za-ma.

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:11.230
Sumi-chan?

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:13.970
Oh no — it's already noon?!

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:15.410
Let's go to lunch!

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:38.480
Why can't girls love one another?

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:45.520
Kazama-san, what did you just say?

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:47.160
Just as I suspected.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.250
Your malady is making itself known again.

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:50.750
Hey! That's rude!

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.560
I've always felt this way.

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:54.450
Always?

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:55.830
Only girls?

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:58.500
I've never liked anyone but girls!

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:01.400
Yeah, yeah, yeah. You're right.

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:07.490
Come on, you two; don't just talk amongst yourselves!

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:11.270
This girl likes girls.

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:16.520
I don't think it's that unusual…

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:23.030
Is that… so?

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.770
Then, you should've gone to an all-girls school.

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:29.790
I tried to.

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:31.040
She didn't get accepted.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:35.040
At the interview, they asked her why she applied.

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:37.540
Because I like cute girls!

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:39.860
Oh dear...

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.060
So, then...

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:47.860
For instance, how about me?

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:52.430
Ah, I'm sorry. I like cute girls.

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:55.690
So, who is it this time?

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:58.190
Secret!

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:29.220
Say, do you have this book?

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:31.830
Y-Yes!

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:33.140
Thank you.

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:39.440
Let's see... I'll call for you when I find it, then.

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:40.590
Okay.

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:44.180
It'll be due on the 20th.

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:47.810
Thank you very much.

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:57.580
What is it, Senpai?

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:03.840
Since this isn't a bookstore,
isn't it a bit weird to say "Thank you very much"?

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:09.160
Kazama-san?

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:12.220
I-It's not weird!

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:13.520
Not at all!

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:49.880
I'm home.

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:51.640
Welcome back.

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:53.480
Thank you.

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:54.340
You're welcome.

00:06:54.340 --> 00:06:57.250
Is there something in particular
you would like to eat tomorrow?

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:00.520
Octopus...

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:01.530
Huh?

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:03.880
N-Nothing! It's fine!

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:48.900
Oh, man...

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:56.040
Well, it <i>is</i> an octopus...

00:07:56.850 --> 00:08:01.410
"Since this isn't a bookstore, isn't it
a bit weird to say 'Thank you very much'?"

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:03.410
That's what she said.

00:08:03.410 --> 00:08:06.170
Isn't she cute? Isn't Senpai cute?

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:08.760
Wasn't it supposed to be a secret?

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:12.660
At first, I just thought her
handwriting was neat and pretty.

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:15.690
Then, I realized just how beautiful
her hands and fingers were.

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:19.990
Her face, her mannerisms,
and her voice are all very feminine!

00:08:19.990 --> 00:08:22.450
She's so cute and beautiful!

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:23.770
It's practically a crime!

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:25.900
Um, I don't quite understand...

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:28.970
Just being near her makes me feel warm.

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:30.470
Her hobbies include reading, making sweets—

00:08:30.470 --> 00:08:32.400
Doesn't she have a boyfriend?

00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:36.110
If she's really that cute.

00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:38.860
Of course she doesn't!

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:46.420
If not a boyfriend, then someone she likes.

00:08:47.470 --> 00:08:49.840
You'll just end up devastated again.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:53.280
It's been like that ever since junior high, Kazama.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:57.680
You delude yourself,
while getting ever more excited.

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:01.410
In the end, you still face rejection.

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:03.670
Why not just call it quits?

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:05.190
It's just a waste of time.

00:09:13.930 --> 00:09:15.170
Perhaps...

00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:19.030
Kazama-san, you're beautiful,
so a boyfriend or two...

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:30.380
I just wanted to have an enjoyable lunch...

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:33.340
Sorry...

00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:46.830
Stupid Sumi-chan...

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:04.870
I-It'll be due on the 21st.

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:09.210
Thank you very much.

00:10:15.910 --> 00:10:18.970
Oh no... I said it again.

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:21.400
"Thank you."

00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:32.520
Senpai, is there someone you like?

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:35.080
N-No, no one...

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:38.440
Actually,  I... Senpai...

00:10:38.440 --> 00:10:40.110
Oh my, truly?

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:45.330
I... like you, too.

00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:08.430
All rise.

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:09.390
Bow.

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:12.770
I'll get it this time!

00:11:13.050 --> 00:11:14.670
Like I said, no running!

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:33.670
President, Vice President?

00:11:35.150 --> 00:11:39.480
Abe-sensei asked to have the
materials for world history ready.

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:42.320
Oh, certainly.

00:11:53.930 --> 00:11:57.190
Murasame-san, did you have a fight with Kazama-san?

00:11:58.860 --> 00:11:59.830
Why?

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:04.450
You two haven't spoken at all today.

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:11.700
Um...

00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:22.610
Thank you...

00:12:26.420 --> 00:12:27.330
No problem.

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:35.190
Murasame-san, you're a nice person.

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:46.730
That's not true... at all.

00:13:01.150 --> 00:13:02.090
Where are we going?

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:03.820
Let's all go sometime soon!
Where are we going?

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:04.230
Let's all go sometime soon!

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:05.130
Huh?

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:08.900
You haven't gone home yet?

00:13:09.370 --> 00:13:14.950
Ah, well... Kazama's still at the library.

00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:17.650
Kiyori!

00:13:19.480 --> 00:13:21.530
Please make sure you reconcile.

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:25.600
Kiyori-chan, let's go!

00:13:25.960 --> 00:13:27.360
I'm coming!

00:13:29.900 --> 00:13:32.700
I don't want to have a gloomy lunch, okay?

00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:43.900
It's nice to have friends.

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:22.630
Make sure to lock up.

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:23.460
Certainly.

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:45.300
I'm finished with the daily log,
so I'll help you.

00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:47.240
Thank you.

00:15:02.610 --> 00:15:05.670
"I like you, too."

00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:11.670
Say, Kazama-san...

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:18.100
Do you have someone you like?

00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:22.200
N-No! Not really!

00:15:27.450 --> 00:15:28.380
I see.

00:15:50.930 --> 00:15:55.600
There is someone in my class who likes you.

00:16:00.280 --> 00:16:05.980
The one to whom I said
"Thank you very much" yesterday.

00:16:07.990 --> 00:16:09.650
He...

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:15.810
...would always come to the library just to see you.

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:22.440
So he asked me...

00:16:24.320 --> 00:16:27.350
...if I could ask you...

00:16:29.600 --> 00:16:33.010
...if there was someone you liked...

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:37.680
Senpai—

00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:01.170
Kazama, are you done?

00:17:15.280 --> 00:17:16.240
Kazama?

00:17:30.470 --> 00:17:35.280
Sumi-chan... S-Senpai...

00:17:37.390 --> 00:17:39.020
Senpai...

00:18:08.550 --> 00:18:10.010
What?

00:18:10.010 --> 00:18:12.400
It's not your fault at all, Kazama.

00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:16.530
But Senpai glared at me so furiously...

00:18:16.790 --> 00:18:19.500
That's what you call undue resentment!

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:23.100
She's such a foolish girl.

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:25.310
Don't cry over that girl anymore.

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:27.160
Don't refer to Senpai as "that girl"!

00:18:27.400 --> 00:18:28.420
You still like her?!

00:18:30.860 --> 00:18:31.960
Well...

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:35.620
I was in love with her just a moment ago.

00:18:39.910 --> 00:18:41.180
You're right...

00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:48.190
After all, no one wants to see their loved one cry.

00:19:12.130 --> 00:19:13.420
I'm sorry...

00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:17.330
...for being such a weird friend.

00:19:19.240 --> 00:19:21.450
Weird and stupid.

00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:23.310
That's mean.

00:19:34.790 --> 00:19:35.990
Sumi-chan...

00:19:38.030 --> 00:19:39.960
...will you be my friend forever?

00:19:44.980 --> 00:19:45.760
Yeah.

00:19:49.720 --> 00:19:52.290
Ah, this is such a drag.

00:19:52.290 --> 00:19:55.880
Am I destined to suffer unrequited
love for all eternity?

00:19:57.250 --> 00:20:02.600
If only the person I like would reciprocate my feelings.

00:20:04.150 --> 00:20:05.360
You're right...

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:11.180
If only...

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:32.460
Kazama-san, that sausage looks delicious!

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:33.750
May I have one?

00:20:35.470 --> 00:20:36.910
Thank you!

00:20:46.150 --> 00:20:49.750
Did you... reconcile?

00:20:53.510 --> 00:20:55.890
What's with this, then?!

00:20:55.890 --> 00:20:59.540
I'm sorry, but it was Sumi-chan's idea.

00:20:59.540 --> 00:21:02.650
It was fun watching your reaction.

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:04.240
Fun?!

00:21:07.260 --> 00:21:09.260
I'll give you some asparagus too.

00:21:10.480 --> 00:21:11.750
You're so mean!

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:13.870
I'll eat it, though.

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:15.260
Eat it, eat it!

00:21:21.080 --> 00:21:21.920
Huh?

00:21:21.940 --> 00:21:23.450
Wh-What?

00:21:23.450 --> 00:21:24.790
What's wrong?

00:23:09.020 --> 00:23:13.370
I understand remembering something and
laughing to yourself, but crying to yourself?

00:23:13.660 --> 00:23:16.260
It's just the movie I saw yesterday.

00:23:16.260 --> 00:23:18.960
Geez, you really startled me.

00:23:28.970 --> 00:23:30.770
This is in return for yesterday.

00:23:31.930 --> 00:23:33.170
Thank you.

00:23:37.940 --> 00:23:40.070
Ah, hello — I'm Akemiya.

00:23:40.070 --> 00:23:41.240
So, all of a sudden you're here?

00:23:41.240 --> 00:23:43.530
B-But this is how it was in the original!

00:23:43.530 --> 00:23:45.040
Fine, I guess...

00:23:45.040 --> 00:23:46.730
So, what's going to happen next?

00:23:49.460 --> 00:23:50.680
There you have it.

00:23:50.680 --> 00:23:52.080
Then, see you next week.
